Workstream ID: calm-change-guide
Title: Document the local interface changes with real before-and-after screenshots
Status: IN_REVIEW
Milestone: Deliver a private screenshot-led change guide and complete page inventory
Dependencies: calm-interface, omscs-specializations
GitHub issue: https://github.com/Zanark/CareerOS/issues/17
Purpose: Explain what the local CareerOS candidate removed, moved, disclosed,
  retained or added. Reuse verified pre-cleanup evidence and capture matching
  current views in disposable workspaces. Distinguish the interface cleanup
  from later academic behavior changes; do not alter the website for the report.

Tasks:
  [x] Establish the published-code baseline and current local source boundary.
  [x] Locate preserved before captures and their original fixture/audit method.
  [x] Review the actual source diff and classify changes across all routes.
  [x] Capture current matched views and on-demand interaction states safely.
  [x] Show later academic additions separately from presentation cleanup.
  [x] Build economical contact sheets, selected crops and explanatory captions.
  [x] Produce a visual guide with a complete page-by-page disposition inventory.
  [x] Inspect offline HTML/PDF, screenshot integrity, provenance and legibility.
  [x] Verify source/data/previews and prepare the same-identity tracking read-back.

Acceptance criteria:
  Every screenshot is a real application capture with explicit source/viewport/
    fixture provenance. Historical before images are not relabelled as fresh.
  Compare matching legacy-empty demonstration state for cleanup views. Show
    cold-start academic defaults separately, not as evidence of text removal.
  Do not read, reset, import or automate the owner's actual browser/profile.
    Demonstration values and public starter examples are not live private records.
  Cover all previously audited normal routes and the new specialization route.
    Selected screenshots illustrate the inventory; do not imply every state or
    every hidden field was individually pictured.
  Clearly distinguish deleted redundancy, contextual help, native disclosures,
    tutorial teaching, navigation movement, unchanged content and new behavior.
  Preserve important warnings, actual study/record content, typography and data
    semantics. Do not equate fewer visible words with proof of preservation.
  Crops/highlights remain labelled derivatives; retain raw frames and never
    redraw controls or fabricate before/after differences.
  The guide works offline with legible screenshot detail, captions and a PDF.
    Use contact sheets and selected detail review instead of excessive image views.
  No application edits, source staging/commit/push/deployment or public image/
    report upload. Preserve user previews and stop only owned temporary helpers.
  Only generic public-safe metadata is mirrored into the original issue/item;
    private paths, screenshots, report bodies and academic values stay local.

